>
  <p>Hermes is a personal, locally hosted AI system that retrieves subscription-related emails from the owner's Gmail account and organizes the information for personal AI-assisted analysis. The application is intended for private use and is not publicly accessible.</p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>The owner authorizes Gmail access through Google OAuth. Hermes runs on the owner's local computer and retrieves subscription-related emails for organization and analysis within the owner's AI workflow.</p>

  <h2>Private use</h2>
  <p>Hermes is operated by Liz Liu for personal use. It does not offer public registration or access to other people's Gmail accounts.</p>
  <p>This website provides public information about Hermes. It does not run Hermes, request Gmail authorization, or receive the owner's emails or OAuth tokens.</p>

  <h2>Privacy and terms</h2>
  <p>Read the <a href="/hermes/privacy">Hermes Privacy Policy</a> for details about data access, storage, use, sharing, and deletion, and the <a href="/hermes/terms">Terms of Service</a> for conditions of use.</p>
